  "task": {
    "objective": "Sustain eight interlinked farms with shared water, seed traits and compost labor; grow and deliver fruit while choosing which fungal resource links to connect, prune or treat as disease routes across a persistent finite valley.",
    "natural_termination": "No natural success or joint-failure terminal. This is a continuing finite world. H=640 truncates the observation window, not a success event; done inputs are absorbing.",
    "interaction": "Neighbor soil imbalances launch visible packets carrying actual withdrawn water and nutrients along root corridors. Wet infected farms can infect those packets and later nonresistant crops at another farm. Pruning cancels the in-flight resource packet and future exchange; grafting, watering, compost transport, shared finite facilities and tool/resource handoffs alter peers' future feasible work.",
    "observation_access": "Fully public native physical world. Every role receives its own ID followed by the same public_keys vector: positions, tools, carried resources, seed/crop traits, soil, links, in-flight packets including infection, shared facilities, weather/calendar and real event/reward components. All entity visibility masks are true; inactive packets are not rendered as present. There is no hidden order, private farm stock or renderer-only information. Group labels and role selection use the same actor/farm state."
  },
